# Array index out of range. Implementation-defined: ed.3 annex E / ed.2
# annex E list "array index out of range" among the errors whose detection
# and handling are implementer-specific (a runtime error, a clamped
# access, or no check at all).
# The records are what IronPLC does. Cycles 0 and 1 are the in-range
# sanity check; the out-of-range read is placed last because it may stop
# the program.
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs: idx
outputs: v ok
status: implementation-defined
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 annex E (array index out of range)
---
0 idx=2 => v=20 ok=TRUE
1 idx=3 => v=30 ok=TRUE
2 idx=4 => trap
